<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrew Jackson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1845">1845</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrew Jackson was an American general and the seventh President of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, serving from 1829 to 1837. He won fame by defeating the British at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a> in 1815 and invaded Spanish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-seminole-war">First Seminole War</a>. As president he signed the Indian Removal Act of 1830, which forced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cherokee">Cherokee</a>, Seminole and other nations west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/andrew-jackson.jpg" alt="Andrew Jackson" width="320" height="398" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ralph Eleaser Whiteside Earl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Andrew_jackson_head_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
